      "reason": "Individually reviewed approximate road-reserve site position. The Council-associated official Walcha visitor map (actual PDF page 1) places its EV icon in the Apsley Street block west of Derby Street near Police Station (1). Council's 25 October 2023 business paper (actual PDF page 107, item 3.3) records NRMA construction on the road reserve adjacent to 10W Apsley Street. The pinned OCM NRMA record identifies 10W Apsley Street, Walcha 2354, matching the complete source address. Its point lies 76.76 m west-southwest (258.07 degrees) of the independently mapped police building and within 1 m of the mapped Apsley Street road line. The complete OSM building/street ways, nodes, tags, coordinates and source hash are fixed; bounded direction, distance and street-corridor checks reproduce this map interpretation. Police is a mapped landmark, not a second charger or operator-point corroboration. The OCM point is an approximate position within the documented street site: neither the schematic visitor map nor this point establishes a surveyed charging bay or side of the road. The old NRMA KML is about 258 m farther south and is not used to corroborate this correction. Dated installation and geographic evidence does not establish present charging availability. All original coordinates, postal fields, address and equipment observations remain unchanged in the original fields."
